{"title":"1992 USAMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find, as a function of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/5/d355fce2af566ceb80d3d58aa61382c5d0bb4c81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, n, \\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"11\" /> the sum of the digits of \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/5/395f3a29a3769af826b23ad1d2ca73fe825dd3d4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[9 \\times 99 \\times 9999 \\times \\cdots \\times \\left( 10^{2^n} - 1 \\right),\\]\" width=\"261\" height=\"22\" /> \nwhere each factor has twice as many digits as the previous one.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1992 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Prove \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/a/c7a719b049c276e55a58cfb22c3e914b3cce1a7f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{\\cos 0^\\circ \\cos 1^\\circ} +  \\frac{1}{\\cos 1^\\circ \\cos 2^\\circ} + \\cdots + \\frac{1}{\\cos 88^\\circ \\cos 89^\\circ} = \\frac{\\cos 1^\\circ}{\\sin^2 1^\\circ}.\\]\" width=\"471\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1992 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For a nonempty set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> of integers, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/acc319088e7b2c4c18a688e6f7434b9bb79984c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sigma(S)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"20\" /> be the sum of the elements of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />. Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/2/a62cf19a8d2c3834650539c60fbf0f46a7cc70d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\{a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_{11}\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"164\" height=\"20\" /> is a set of positive integers with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/8/9d86a5555798f6e24fec0555094fa870ce6c2c2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 &lt; a_2 &lt; \\cdots &lt; a_{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"149\" height=\"12\" /> and that, for each positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/4/8c49ffd9a5fdfba3bc289de7400843c0294e5c33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\le 1500$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"70\" height=\"15\" />, there is a subset <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/8/0a8d87544d694d3429302b7a867c3a06da7e23b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sigma(S) = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"18\" />. What is the smallest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/5/f659be762622558799a9119468b5008cb1b27f78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"22\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1992 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Chords <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/9/d59f5d75cc27d504ede022aab803742e799709f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AA&#39;$\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/a/c2ae0e30605dc87c83aecb3f588afa7129bee6aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BB&#39;$\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/b/44b7058f8a28ca225136b284b337138a54e39e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CC&#39;$\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of a sphere meet at an interior point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> but are not contained in the same plane.  The sphere through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is tangent to the sphere through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/1090530ae883b627e090bfb5e450ef796febca40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c71f19552a05ee5e2b31e94aff3fb986884bf31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/7/9b798193cb94562989018728e1151587c618655b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.  Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/b/3ab3e22ac87b9427dec760c5f02246bb7005e647.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AA&#39;=BB&#39;=CC&#39;$\" width=\"146\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1992 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/0/9e048a9db04ffc89eec3e0d78777919f12df3aeb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" />be a polynomial with complex coefficients which is of degree <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/3/b03ee1a88cbf56bb44f636da026ae2ec0ee1f98f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1992$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> and has distinct zeros.Prove that there exists complex numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/f/ebf1813c975a0bce0e83c65efe678d3c365a532b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1,a_2,\\cdots,a_{1992}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"120\" height=\"11\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/0/9e048a9db04ffc89eec3e0d78777919f12df3aeb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> divides the polynomial\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/f/0ffcefbb0adb249c4f35a8ea1e8045b9d4ccff33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\cdots\\left(\\left(z-a_1\\right)^2-a_2\\right)^2\\cdots-a_{1991}\\right)^2-a_{1992}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"336\" height=\"46\" /></center>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1992 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_USAMO\" title=\"1992 USAMO\">1992 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1992\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_USAMO\" title=\"1991 USAMO\">1991 USAMO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_USAMO\" title=\"1993 USAMO\">1993 USAMO</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1992 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1992 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1992 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1992 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1992 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017200941\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.030 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.047 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 205/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1209/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 60/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5646/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   11.928      1 -total\n 57.21%    6.824      1 Template:USAMO_box\n 41.02%    4.893      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache wit